fact('F-authority','The instance currently processes inputs in its selected role and term; a leader role results from quorum election support. This is local authority state, not proof of an unexpired external lease.',{'node':'Local node ID','epoch':'raft.Term'},'Configured voters and serialized term dispatch; same-term role loss remains possible.',['raft.Term','raft.Vote','raft.state','raft.lead'],'Term and Vote are emitted for persistence; role and leader are volatile.','Restart loads term/vote then becomes follower.',['M-election','M-dispatch','M-reset','M-init'],invalidators=['B-authority','B-config','B-recovery'])
fact('F-match','Within leader tracking, peer Match is the highest acknowledged matching prefix known for that peer. Self Match is initialized at reset to local tail and later updated by durable self-ack; the current-term commitment check prevents that initialization alone committing an older tail.',{'leader':'Local node ID and leader term','peer':'Progress map key'},'Current leader epoch and peer Progress membership; not a heartbeat or client completion fact.',['Progress.Match','Progress.Next'],'Volatile evidence; remote support assumes durable response contract.','Reset rebuilds peer progress rather than loading prior Match.',['M-reset','M-support','M-tracker','M-send'],invalidators=['B-authority','B-recovery'],reinterpreters=['B-config'])
fact('F-commit','The local committed watermark identifies an immutable accepted prefix eligible for ordered application, subject to local stability and snapshot handling. It does not assert application completed.',{'instance':'Local node ID','prefix':'Committed log index and associated log history'},'Monotonic within the instance; leader quorum/current-term advancement, follower accepted leader propagation, or committed snapshot/recovery.',['raftLog.committed','HardState.Commit'],'HardState and log/snapshot are written by caller according to Ready contract.','Load saved Commit and snapshot boundary; reject inconsistent bounds.',['M-log-commit','M-log-append','M-follower-log','M-init','M-config'],reinterpreters=['B-recovery'])
fact('F-config','The active configuration records incoming and optional outgoing voters, learner roles and whether the joint state requests automatic exit. AutoLeave records policy, not an already-enqueued exit proposal or completed transition.',{'instance':'Local node ID','configuration':'Applied ConfChange sequence or restored ConfState'},'From committed configuration application or initialization/restoration until the next configuration update. Quorum formation uses both sets while outgoing voters remain.',['ProgressTracker.Config','ConfState.AutoLeave','Config.Voters','Config.LearnersNext'],'Configuration is represented in committed history and recorded ConfState snapshots by the caller.','confchange.Restore rebuilds sets and AutoLeave from ConfState; Bootstrap establishes initial peers.',['M-config','M-changer','M-conf-restore','M-bootstrap','M-conf-contract','M-auto-contract'],invalidators=['B-config','B-recovery'])
fact('F-applied','The raft instance has recorded acknowledgment of application progress through applied. It is internal accounting; in normal mode the Node interface also permits early Advance before application finishes.',{'instance':'Local node ID','prefix':'Applied index'},'Caller-ordered application/acknowledgment; term-independent committed work may acknowledge after authority changes.',['raftLog.applied','raftLog.applying','raftLog.applyingEntsSize'],'Not separately persisted by raft; caller supplies restart Applied and application state.','newRaft applies configured Applied to recovered log bounds.',['M-api','M-dispatch','M-log-pointers','M-apply-response','M-init'])
roles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']
summaries={
'A1':('Leader appends qualified proposals, counts durable append support from configured voters under current-term commit validation, and propagates committed prefixes; followers preserve committed history and reject incompatible prefixes.',['raft.stepLeader','raft.handleAppendEntries','ProgressTracker.Committed'],['M-proposal','M-support','M-follower-log','M-joint-quorum']),
'A2':('Tick/Campaign, vote quorum and term dispatch acquire or relinquish local leadership. Reset invalidates transient support; transfer suppresses proposals until takeover or timeout while established committed state survives.',['raft.Step','raft.campaign','raft.reset','raft.tickHeartbeat'],['M-election','M-dispatch','M-reset','M-transfer']),
'A3':('Restart and snapshot handling rebuild history and participant configuration; replication probes, rejection hints and snapshots let lagging peers rejoin.',['newRaft','raft.restore','raft.maybeSendSnapshot'],['M-init','M-restore','M-replicate']),
'A4':('Committed configuration application changes voters and learner roles through simple/joint validation; AutoLeave is an implementation-owned proposal continuation triggered by acknowledged application.',['raft.applyConfChange','confchange.Changer','raft.appliedTo'],['M-config','M-changer','M-auto','M-conf-contract']),
'A5':('Ready selects committed work with size/stability/snapshot bounds; caller application and Advance or local-worker response update applied accounting. Actual business state execution is outside this library.',['RawNode.Ready','RawNode.Advance','MsgStorageApplyResp'],['M-ready','M-apply-response','M-log-apply','M-api']),
'A6':('Storage and unstable overlay reconstruct log history; Ready separates durability-sensitive replies from immediate messages. In-repository MemoryStorage supplies a volatile backend; disk IO and durable writes are external caller duties.',['Storage','MemoryStorage','RawNode.readyWithoutAccept','unstable.stableTo'],['M-storage-contract','M-memory-storage','M-unstable','M-storage-response']),
'A7':('Node/RawNode exposes submission, read-index and completion APIs. Submission may be lost; caller retry/correlation and application through read index are needed for endpoint semantics.',['Node.Propose','Node.ReadIndex','ReadState'],['M-api','M-read-tracker','M-node-loop'])}
activities=[dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary=v[0],entry_points=v[1],source_ids=v[2]) for a,v in summaries.items()]
mapdoc=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured go.etcd.io/raft/v3 library: serialized raft state machine, Node/RawNode wrappers, quorum/configuration tracking, log/unstable and MemoryStorage. Production network, durable disk and business application are caller-owned; in-repository implementations are included where read.',protocol_contexts=['Local raft instance with monotonic terms, log entry identity (term,index), simple/joint voter configurations and optional learners.'],external_interfaces=['Node and RawNode','Storage','Ready/Advance or AsyncStorageWrites worker messages'],ownership=['Node.run serializes state; RawNode requires caller serialization.','Caller owns transport, durable writes, ordered application, periodic Tick, and retries.'],variants=['PreVote and CheckQuorum','ReadOnlySafe and lease-based reads','Normal Ready/Advance and AsyncStorageWrites','Simple, joint implicit and joint explicit configuration','StepDownOnRemoval option'],source_ids=['M-boundary','M-api','M-raw-api','M-async-contract','M-config']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[
 dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo -> transfer rejection -> tickHeartbeat abort',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-auto-leave','B-transfer','B-application'],reason='Specific unresolved continuation premise: a heartbeat-only Advance does not acknowledge applied entries, so the comment promising retry on next advance needs a legal-history discriminator.',source_ids=['M-auto','M-election','M-apply-response','M-advance','M-transfer-abort'],high_consequence=True),
 dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig -> maybeCommit',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-config','B-formation','B-authority'],reason='Unlike append-response commitment this path does not release pending reads. Whether it can establish the first current-term commit with pending reads is unresolved; campaign forbids committed unapplied config, which is concrete counterevidence. Read request loss is expressly permitted.',source_ids=['M-config','M-support','M-election','M-api'],high_consequence=False),
 dict(entry_point='Node.Advance before finishing application / ApplyConfChange',disposition='deferred',reason='Node interface permits early Advance; ordering relative to configuration application and automatic exit needs separate contract investigation. The selected transfer question will apply configuration before Advance.',source_ids=['M-api','M-auto','M-config'],high_consequence=True),
 dict(entry_point='rafttest.InteractionEnv storage/transport drivers',disposition='deferred',reason='In-repository test drivers were located but not inspected; no helper legality or scheduling guarantees are assumed.',source_ids=[],high_consequence=False),
 dict(entry_point='Production network/disk/business application',disposition='externalized',reason='Library boundary explicitly delegates IO and application; only sourced caller contracts, not a deployment implementation, are available.',source_ids=['M-boundary','M-ready-contract'],high_consequence=True)
])
def path(ex,b,f,s):return dict(explanation=ex,behavior_ids=b,fact_ids=f,source_ids=s)
mapdoc['core_overview']=dict(status='usable',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Whether automatic leave can lose its continuation when transfer suppresses the final application-triggered attempt and later times out.','Whether configuration-triggered commitment can be the first current-term commit with pending reads, despite campaign restrictions.','Early-Advance configuration ordering, detailed membership/removal read interactions, and broader concurrent snapshot/apply histories remain uninvestigated variants.'],rationale='Representative formation and authority paths were traced through producers, quorum aggregation, persistence, dispatch, configuration, recovery and application. This is a navigable initial explanation, not full path coverage or defect evidence.',
 formation=path('A leader assigns term/index to proposals, emits log appends and defers its self-ack until persistence. Followers check predecessor identity, preserve committed entries, append the uncommitted suffix and return durability-dependent support. In the leader term, known-peer positive replies update Match; voting majority (both halves if joint) yields a candidate index, and matching the current term permits committed advancement. Broadcast append and Match-capped heartbeat propagate the decision. Ready then exposes the ordered committed prefix subject to snapshot and local-stability/application-size constraints; caller application and acknowledgment consume it. Rejection hints, heartbeat-driven empty appends and snapshot fallback support recovery without treating activity as matched history.',['B-formation','B-follow-log','B-persistence','B-application','B-config','B-recovery'],['F-match','F-commit','F-config'],['M-send','M-proposal','M-support','M-replicate','M-follower-log','M-joint-quorum','M-log-commit','M-log-apply']),
 context=path('Election starts only from a promotable instance with no committed unapplied configuration. PreVote probes without raising term; real campaign increments term and counts persisted self/peer votes using current voter sets and log freshness. Higher-term dispatch or loss of quorum can relinquish authority; same-term leader traffic demotes candidates. Reset clears transient vote/read/peer-progress state but retains log and committed decisions. Older network replies are rejected; append-storage completions are term-qualified, whereas committed snapshot/apply completions survive term changes. Leadership transfer first catches up a tracked voter, then sends TimeoutNow and suppresses proposals until takeover or timeout.',['B-authority','B-transfer','B-persistence','B-recovery'],['F-authority','F-config','F-commit'],['M-election','M-dispatch','M-reset','M-role-handlers','M-transfer','M-storage-response']),
 connection=path('A2 qualifies whose A1 support can be consumed: term dispatch and reset prevent a new leader from aggregating old-term replication replies, and the current-term entry requirement ties retained older log history to fresh quorum support. Committed decisions are term-independent, so application/storage snapshot acknowledgment may complete after leadership changes; overwritable append history instead needs a current-term durability attestation. Applied configuration changes alter the voter sets used by both election and replication quorums, while campaign blocks unapplied committed membership. Automatic joint exit is a separate application-triggered proposal, so recorded AutoLeave and recorded application do not themselves mean exit was scheduled. Pending read-only acknowledgments reset with authority; the pre-current-term request queue survives reset and is reprocessed through current-term read logic on an append-response commit.',['B-authority','B-formation','B-persistence','B-config','B-auto-leave','B-application','B-client-read'],['F-authority','F-match','F-commit','F-config','F-applied'],['M-reset','M-dispatch','M-log-commit','M-storage-response','M-config','M-auto','M-election','M-pending-read']))
